Comment (cmd/factory-agent/host_test.go:442):
**[Nit] The test panics when the child never starts**

When `cmd.CombinedOutput()` fails before the child starts, `cmd.ProcessState` is nil. The exit-3 check guards against that, but the next line, `cmd.ProcessState.Sys()`, doesn't, so the test panics where it should fail with the start error.

**Why:** It affects only how a test reports a failure that is very unlikely (re-executing the test binary). It's a one-line guard.
**Fix:** Before the exit-code check: `if cmd.ProcessState == nil { t.Fatalf("running the child: %v", err) }`.
**Severity basis:** no rule matched; decision tree: none of the tree questions.

